  "_audit_note": "18 Aug 2026 (overhaul Block 0): ArsenalFC-Audit added — designed 12 Aug in INSTALL_TASKS.ps1, never installed live, registered today (13:10 daily, no catch-up). ArsenalFC-BugMuseum and ArsenalFC-Mutants stay designed-but-not-installed on purpose (audit-suite cost organs; no check requires them; Block 7 runs mutagen by hand) — an installer re-run would register them, and this file should gain them in that same commit.",
  "_slots_doc": "OVERHAUL Block 6 (18 Aug 2026) — THE DAY-KEY LAW: name → {organ, verb, at (HH:MM or [HH:MM,…] for multi-trigger rows), interval (ISO-8601, null = once-a-slot), dow ([\"sun\"…] for WEEKLY rows — a Sunday slot woken on Monday keys Sunday; null otherwise), daemon, enabled}, snapshotted from the LIVE Task Scheduler by `node scripts/herd.mjs slots`. daykey.mjs reads THIS map (never a 2–5 s PowerShell spawn per run) so an organ launched by Task Scheduler in a catch-up burst keys its day to ITS SLOT: an ENABLED, ONCE-A-SLOT, NON-DAEMON row → slotDate(at, now); interval rows and daemons stay on the clock by design; a chain child takes the conductor’s token first. The watchman WARNs task-slot-drift when a live trigger no longer matches this map — move a task, re-run `herd slots`, paste, commit together (this file’s own rule).",
